WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.735
Mastery Starter 3.0.

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.710
New to Lending & Leverage?

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:05.770
Start here.

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.857
In about ten minutes, you'll go from

00:00:07.857 --> 00:00:09.550
zero to ready for this module.

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:13.877
Lending markets let you earn interest by lending, or

00:00:13.877 --> 00:00:16.862
borrow against what you own without selling it.

00:00:16.862 --> 00:00:20.205
Borrowing comes with one hard rule: if your collateral

00:00:20.205 --> 00:00:23.427
falls too far, it's sold automatically, at a penalty.

00:00:24.727 --> 00:00:27.212
Collateral: what you lock up to borrow.

00:00:27.212 --> 00:00:30.637
LTV: debt ÷ collateral value.

00:00:30.637 --> 00:00:34.872
Health factor: your safety margin; below 1 means liquidation.

00:00:34.872 --> 00:00:38.477
Liquidation: forced sale of collateral to repay debt.

00:00:38.477 --> 00:00:41.322
Utilisation: how much of a pool is borrowed.

00:00:42.622 --> 00:00:44.837
First, Modules 0–2.

00:00:44.837 --> 00:00:46.633
And finally, Comfort using a

00:00:46.633 --> 00:00:48.182
DEX on a low-fee network.

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:52.986
Supply $20 of USDC to a blue-chip lending

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:57.207
market, read its utilisation, then withdraw it.

00:00:57.207 --> 00:00:58.397
No borrowing yet.

00:00:59.697 --> 00:01:04.072
Beginner: Supplies stablecoins and reads utilisation and rates.

00:01:04.072 --> 00:01:06.684
Practitioner: Borrows with HF ≥ 2

00:01:06.684 --> 00:01:09.212
and a written defence ladder.

00:01:09.212 --> 00:01:12.130
Master: Runs correlated loops and perps with

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:15.308
computed liquidation prices and break-even rates.

00:01:16.608 --> 00:01:19.964
You've mastered this module when you can open, monitor

00:01:19.964 --> 00:01:23.443
and unwind a borrow without ever approaching liquidation.

00:01:24.743 --> 00:01:27.258
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:01:27.258 --> 00:01:30.753
Next up, Lesson 3.1: How lending markets work.
